# The emulated MCU only (docs/FIRMWARE.md): platform, firmware image and reset behaviour, with
# no I/O wiring and not started. openfleet.resc adds the TCP UART and starts it for the
# gateway; the Robot Framework tests (firmware/renode/tests) add a file UART and drive it in
# emulated time. Emulated, not a board.
# Variables (set before including): $bin (ELF), $repl (platform).
$bin ?= @/src/firmware/build/openfleet-fw.elf
$repl ?= @/src/firmware/renode/openfleet-f4.repl

# Sync emulated time every 1 ms instead of every 0.1 ms: about 1 host core instead of 1.6 on
# the dev Mac (measured), still finer than the firmware's 1 ms tick and 20 ms sampling.
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.001"

mach create "mcu2"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl

# What a reset does (the IWDG requests one): reload the image and restart from its vector
# table. SRAM is not cleared, as on the real chip, so the boot record survives.
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""
runMacro $reset
